# Retrieval labels: question -> the note(s) that actually hold the answer.
#
# Scored by eval_retrieval.py, which reports where the target landed in the
# fused ranking (capability) and whether it survived truncation to keep_k
# (what the 3B actually sees). No LLM judge, deterministic, seconds per arm.
#
# LABELING METHOD. Candidates were proposed by scoring the gold set's
# must_cover FACT text against the index, never the question wording, because
# the question wording is the thing under test. Every proposal was then
# confirmed by reading the note and finding the fact stated in it. Questions
# whose target could not be established are omitted rather than guessed; a
# wrong label manufactures a regression that no amount of tuning can fix.
#
# label_method values:
#   card    the fact is in the note's definition card / frontmatter (Founded:, Hq:)
#   body    the fact is stated in the note body, verified line read
#   hard    target confirmed, but the question shares almost no vocabulary with
#           the note. These are the diagnostic cases: they are what semantic
#           search is FOR, and they are where BM25 provably cannot help.
{"id": "gallaudet_location", "set": "factual_gold", "question": "Where is Gallaudet University?", "expect_sources": ["Organizations/Gallaudet University.md"], "label_method": "card", "evidence": "Founded: 1864 ... Federally chartered Deaf university in Washington DC"}
{"id": "gallaudet_founded", "set": "factual_gold", "question": "What year was Gallaudet University founded?", "expect_sources": ["Organizations/Gallaudet University.md"], "label_method": "card", "evidence": "Founded: 1864"}
