# --- gold_questions: analytic, multi-fact. expect_sources is ANY-OF: several
# notes legitimately hold parts of a 6-fact answer, so the honest question is
# "did at least one canonical note reach the window", not "which single note".
# Question text is copied VERBATIM from gold_questions.jsonl: scoring a
# paraphrase would measure a question the system is never asked.
# content_gap lists facts NO note in the vault supports. Reported, never authored.
{"id": "language_deprivation_1", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "Our pediatrician told us that once our deaf son gets his cochlear implant he really won't need to learn to sign, and honestly I've heard that starting ASL now could slow down his spoken English. Is that right, or would waiting on sign language actually cost him something?", "expect_sources": ["LanguageDeprivationAgent/Core/What Is Language Deprivation.md", "LanguageDeprivationAgent/Core/Cochlear Implant Pathways and Risk.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
{"id": "language_deprivation_2", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "I'm a graduate student and I keep reading that deaf kids who didn't get a full language early on can struggle later with things like planning and memory. What is actually going on developmentally, and which researcher's work should I be citing on this?", "expect_sources": ["LanguageDeprivationAgent/Core/What Is Language Deprivation.md", "Sources/Language Deprivation/Hall 2017 - What You Dont Know Can Hurt You.md", "People/Wyatte C. Hall.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
{"id": "critical_period_1", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "My cousin keeps telling me our deaf toddler will pick up signing whenever she's good and ready, so honestly, is there any real harm in just holding off on ASL until she's a bit older?", "expect_sources": ["LanguageDeprivationAgent/Core/Critical Period and Brain.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
{"id": "critical_period_2", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "Our audiologist wants us to focus on a cochlear implant and spoken English first and skip signing for now to avoid confusing our baby, but I keep reading warnings about timing, so what does the science actually say about how waiting affects a deaf child's language development?", "expect_sources": ["LanguageDeprivationAgent/Core/Critical Period and Brain.md", "LanguageDeprivationAgent/Core/Cochlear Implant Pathways and Risk.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
{"id": "asl_full_language_1", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "My mother-in-law keeps insisting that what Deaf people do with their hands is basically English acted out, so it doesn't really count as a language of its own. Is she right?", "expect_sources": ["Concepts/American Sign Language.md", "People/Robbin Battison.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
{"id": "asl_full_language_2", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "I just got a Deaf student who signs, and I earnestly want to understand what linguists have actually established that makes ASL a complete language on par with spoken ones rather than a simplified communication system. Can you walk me through it?", "expect_sources": ["Concepts/American Sign Language.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
{"id": "bilingual_bimodal_1", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "My baby was just identified as deaf and her pediatrician says we should pour everything into speech therapy and worry about reading later. Is there any real harm in raising her with sign language and written English side by side from the very start instead?", "expect_sources": ["LanguageDeprivationAgent/Core/Bilingual Bimodal Protective Factors.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
{"id": "bilingual_bimodal_2", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "Isn't teaching a deaf kid ASL and English at the same time just doubling the workload and setting both languages up to lag? Why do Deaf schools insist on running the two together rather than committing to one?", "expect_sources": ["LanguageDeprivationAgent/Core/Bilingual Bimodal Protective Factors.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
{"id": "deaf_gain_1", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "The audiologist keeps describing my toddler's deafness only as a loss we need to correct, and it makes me uneasy. Is there a serious way of thinking that treats growing up deaf as adding something valuable to a child's life rather than just a shortfall?", "expect_sources": ["Concepts/Deaf Gain.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
{"id": "deaf_gain_2", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "A friend mentioned there's a phrase first spoken by a Deaf performance artist and later developed by two scholars that deliberately turns the whole idea of 'hearing loss' upside down. Who originated it and what is it actually claiming?", "expect_sources": ["Concepts/Deaf Gain.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
{"id": "crpd_language_rights_1", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "A relative keeps insisting that treating sign language as a 'real language' with equal standing is just feel-good political correctness with no legal weight behind it. Is there actually a binding international agreement that backs the idea that signed languages count as full languages?", "expect_sources": ["Concepts/CRPD.md", "LanguageDeprivationAgent/Core/CRPD Article 24 and Sign Language Peoples.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
{"id": "crpd_language_rights_2", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "My daughter is deaf and her school keeps framing signing as an optional therapy service they can cut when budgets are tight. Does any human rights treaty actually say she has a right to be educated in a signed language rather than it being a favor they choose to grant?", "expect_sources": ["LanguageDeprivationAgent/Core/CRPD Article 24 and Sign Language Peoples.md", "CRPD/Article 24 Education.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
{"id": "legal_recognition_1", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "Our government just passed a law that officially names our national sign language, so does that mean Deaf people in our country now have everything they need?", "expect_sources": ["Sources/De Meulder 2015 - Legal Recognition of Sign Languages.md", "Sources/De Meulder 2014 - UNCRPD and Sign Language Peoples.md"], "label_method": "concept"}
