{"id": "gallaudet_1", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "My daughter is Deaf, and her IEP team keeps mentioning a school in Washington, D.C. where every class is taught in sign language. What is that place and why would it be a good fit for her?", "expect_sources": ["LanguageDeprivationAgent/Researcher Briefs/Gallaudet Research Ecosystem.md", "Organizations/Gallaudet University.md"], "label_method": "concept", "content_gap": ["ASL and English as the languages of instruction and campus life", "access designed in from the outset rather than requested"], "question_defect": "premise is off: an IEP team for a school-age child would name the Clerc Center demonstration schools KDES and MSSD, both in DC and both bilingual, not a university. DMV school notes therefore outrank the university note legitimately."}
{"id": "gallaudet_2", "set": "gold_questions", "question": "Honestly, doesn't sending a deaf teenager to a college only for deaf people just wall them off from the hearing world instead of preparing them to live in it?", "expect_sources": ["LanguageDeprivationAgent/Researcher Briefs/Gallaudet Research Ecosystem.md", "Organizations/Gallaudet University.md"], "label_method": "concept", "content_gap": ["the 1988 Deaf President Now protest", "I. King Jordan appointed as first Deaf president"], "question_defect": "UNANSWERABLE as scored: 'Deaf President Now', 'King Jordan' and the 1988 protest have ZERO occurrences anywhere in the vault, yet the rubric requires that fact. No retrieval change can recover it."}
